cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use HealGen in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "HealGen: Claim-Level Evidence-Sufficiency-Guided Self-Healing Inference for Factual LLM Generation"
abstract: >-
  HealGen is a draft-first self-healing inference architecture for factual
  large language model generation.  It decides, per atomic claim, whether to
  trust it, retrieve evidence for it, or repair it locally, using a
  claim-level risk estimator, an evidence-sufficiency predictor gating
  retrieval, a dynamic claim-evidence graph, and localized repair, all driven
  by one validated NLI judge.  The repository also implements the associated
  evaluation protocol: frozen shared evidence pools per question, a gold-only
  scoring condition, a pre-registered judge-validation gate, and scoring of
  the emitted answer rather than private intermediate state.
